From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:38:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] airconv: Let a simdgroup with no live lane run wave ops over
 its helpers.

A pixel shader without [WaveOpsIncludeHelperLanes] masked its wave operations to the non-helper lanes (0041). Once a waterfall loop's covered lanes had left, the helpers that remained got an empty mask: WaveReadLaneFirst read lane 32 and WaveActiveMin the identity, so they never left the loop, a GPU hang without a bound. Such a simdgroup now runs the operation over all its lanes, as Metal does; covered lanes' results are unchanged. Found by the SM 6.8 final review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.hpp | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp b/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp
index 2df559d..8ed4de8 100644
--- a/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp
+++ b/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp
@@ -292,7 +292,14 @@ llvm::Value *Lowering::WaveLanes() {
 }
 
 llvm::Value *Lowering::Participates() {
-  return HelpersLeftOut() ? ir.CreateNot(Simd(ir, "air.simd_is_helper_thread", ir.getInt1Ty(), {})) : ir.getTrue();
+  if (!HelpersLeftOut())
+    return ir.getTrue();
+  auto live = ir.CreateNot(Simd(ir, "air.simd_is_helper_thread", ir.getInt1Ty(), {}));
+  // A simdgroup whose active lanes are all helpers (its covered lanes have left a loop, or a discard demoted them) runs
+  // the operation over them all, as Metal does: D3D leaves a helper's wave results undefined, but a loop waiting on a
+  // wave result must still end for it. Masked to nothing, a waterfall loop's helpers never leave it (a GPU hang).
+  auto none = ir.CreateICmpEQ(Simd(ir, "air.simd_ballot.i64", ir.getInt64Ty(), {live}), ir.getInt64(0));
+  return ir.CreateOr(live, none);
 }
 
 // The 64-bit lock path (spec 3.8), from 32-bit atomics, fences and simdgroup votes; never Metal's 64-bit atomics, which
diff --git a/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.hpp b/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.hpp
index 4ec881c..7a09ca2 100644
--- a/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.hpp
+++ b/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.hpp
@@ -107,7 +107,8 @@ private:
   // The lanes taking part in a wave operation at the insert point: the i64 ballot of the non-helper lanes when helpers
   // are left out, nullptr otherwise (nothing is masked). Emitted at each operation: divergence changes it.
   llvm::Value *WaveLanes();
-  // i1: this lane takes part, !helper when helpers are left out, true otherwise.
+  // i1: this lane takes part. When helpers are left out: a non-helper lane, or any lane of a simdgroup with no active
+  // non-helper lane; true otherwise.
   llvm::Value *Participates();
 
   // Compute shaders, which have no air.dfdx (spec 3.3): the derivative of float `v` (scalar or vector) across its quad,
